{"packet_id":"D041-01","doc_id":"D041","jurisdiction":"Los Angeles, CA","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Los Angeles RSO legal reasons for eviction and relocation assistance","requirement":"A landlord may end an RSO tenancy only for the ordinance's legal reasons for eviction. At-fault causes include nonpayment, nuisance or damage, illegal use and unapproved subtenants; no-fault causes include owner or family move-in, resident manager, demolition, government order and conversion to affordable housing, and require relocation assistance.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, plus replacement units under LAMC 151.28: apartments, condominiums, townhomes, duplexes, two or more single-family units on a parcel, ADUs, JADUs, and mobile homes.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"covered","op":"on_or_before","date":"1978-10-01","basis":"construction"},{"type":"other","role":"exempt","text":"Luxury exemption where the monthly rent charged on or before May 31, 1978 qualifies"}],"per_tenancy":"Condominium and townhome rent is not regulated for tenancies commenced after December 31, 1995.","coverage_quotes":["Generally, the RSO applies to rental properties that were first built on or before October 1, 1978, as well as replacement units under"]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Los Angeles Municipal Code § 151.09","quoted_span":"No-fault evictions require the payment of relocation assistance","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
